  volume    =  12,
  number    =  1,
  pages     =  5169,
  abstract  = "To produce consistent sensory perception, neurons must maintain
               stable representations of sensory input. However, neurons in many
               regions exhibit progressive drift across days. Longitudinal
               studies have found stable responses to artificial stimuli across
               sessions in visual areas, but it is unclear whether this
               stability extends to naturalistic stimuli. We performed chronic
               2-photon imaging of mouse V1 populations to directly compare the
               representational stability of artificial versus naturalistic
               visual stimuli over weeks. Responses to gratings were highly
