  number    =  51,
  pages     = "e2018422118",
  abstract  = "The observation of place cells has suggested that the hippocampus
               plays a special role in encoding spatial information. However,
               place cell responses are modulated by several nonspatial
               variables and reported to be rather unstable. Here, we propose a
               memory model of the hippocampus that provides an interpretation
               of place cells consistent with these observations. We hypothesize
               that the hippocampus is a memory device that takes advantage of
               the correlations between sensory experiences to generate
