  journal  = "Science",
  volume   =  303,
  number   =  5664,
  pages    = "1634--1640",
  abstract = "To what extent do all brains work alike during natural conditions?
              We explored this question by letting five subjects freely view
              half an hour of a popular movie while undergoing functional brain
              imaging. Applying an unbiased analysis in which spatiotemporal
              activity patterns in one brain were used to ``model'' activity in
