               Several authors have speculated that ``maps'' and ``remapping''
               form the physiological substrates for context and context
               shifting. One difficulty with this definition is that it is
               exclusively spatial; it can only be inferred when an animal
               locomotes in an enclosure. There are five aims for this article.
