                 task-relevant information encoded across the neuronal
                 population. Effects of conflict were weaker and more
                 heterogeneous in the dorsolateral prefrontal cortex (dlPFC),
                 suggesting that dACC’s role in conflict processing may be
                 somewhat specialized. Overall, these results support the theory
                 that conflict biases competition between sensorimotor
                 transformation processes occurring in dACC.",
  month       =  mar,
  year        =  2020
}

@ARTICLE{Delarazan2025-bd,
  title     = "Narrative coherence warps the timeline of recalled naturalistic
