              traditional measures of aperiodic neural timescales are influenced
              by oscillations. This makes it difficult to distinguish between
              oscillatory and timescale effects in cognition. Here, we analyzed
              electroencephalography (EEG) data from participants performing a
              cognitive control task that manipulated the amount of
              task-relevant contextual information, called task abstraction.
              Critically, we separated aperiodic neural timescales from the
              confounding influence of oscillatory power. We hypothesized that
