  volume    =  50,
  number    =  3,
  pages     = "478--494",
  abstract  = "Many studies suggest that information about past experience, or
               episodic memory, is divided into discrete units called
               ``events.'' Yet we can often remember experiences that span
               multiple events. Events that occur in close succession might
               simply be linked because of their proximity to one another, but
